{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules","id":1043488,"title":"Question about Spirit rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-04T05:26:31-08:00","id":1043488,"title":"Question about Spirit rules","content":"Hello everyone.<br /> <br /> I am reading the spirit rules from the Forsaken core in 2nd edition and got some parts i dont understand.<br /> <br /> First i dont quite understand how you kill a spirit. So spirits that get all their lethal/aggravated corpus track get discorporated and appear near a resonant condition in hibernation unless they also loose all their essence.<br /> <br /> However on page 186 says that physical attacks on manifest spirits (meaning in twilight right?) or in the hisil deal only bashing. So unless you (a werewolf) outrank the spirit or uses its banes the only way to fill that track is by overflowing its corpus track with bashing until it also becomes lethal?<br /> <br /> On page 186 it says only spirits can be attack other spirits in twilight, does that mean a manifest spirit in invulnerable to werewolf attacks unless it outranks it or uses it banes? But page 185 on banes says that banes only cause lethal damage on spirits on twilight that arent manifested. Doesn't a spirit has to be manifested to BE in twilight? Because it also says manifested spirit touching the bane eat aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> So how hibernation works? it says that the spirit goes into twilight and can act and they can be destroyed there. But as i said above the rules on page 186 says only spirits can attack spirits on twilight so to effectively kill a spirit on twilight another spirit should A) Know about the hibernating spirit. B) Go into twilight and attack it. So that mean a werewolf cant kill a spirit permanently ever?<br /> <br /> On page 184 on &quot;Spirit and Reaching&quot; sidebar it says spirit on a locus that matches its resonance heals twice as fast however i cant find how fast they normally heal.<br /> <br /> About influences, how do they works. Says you got 3 in influences &quot;dog&quot; that means i can only do either:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Strengthen a dog &quot;1 minute per success&quot; (influence effect 1, duration 0)</li> <li>Strengthen a dog &quot;10 minute per success&quot; (influence effect 1, duration 1)</li> <li>Strengthen a dog &quot;1 Hour per success&quot; (influence effect 1, duration 2) and pay 1 additional essence</li> <li>Manipulate a dog &quot;1 minute per success&quot; (influence effect 2, duration 0)</li> <li>Manipulate a dog &quot;10 minute per success&quot; (influence effect 2, duration 1)</li> <li>Control a dog &quot;1 minute per success&quot; (Influence effect 3, duration 0)</li> </ol><br /> So that means a rank 5 spirit cant permanently create a example of its influence?<br /> <br /> About Claimed, it says claimed gain influences of their spirit but loose the numina but can develop Dread powers. It doesnt say however how much dread power they gain.<br /> <br /> And finally the books seem to indicate that whenever it refers to a spirit materialize it truth it means a spirit is in twilight so it cant be seen by normal humans?<br /> <br /> Thanks for any answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T06:19:30-08:00","id":1043506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules#post1043488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However on page 186 says that physical attacks on manifest spirits (meaning in twilight right?) or in the hisil deal only bashing. So unless you (a werewolf) outrank the spirit or uses its banes the only way to fill that track is by overflowing its corpus track with bashing until it also becomes lethal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, yes. I'm not super clear if the whole predator's jaws things is supposed to do lethal to Spirits by default, but I don't think so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules#post1043488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On page 186 it says only spirits can be attack other spirits in twilight, does that mean a manifest spirit in invulnerable to werewolf attacks unless it outranks it or uses it banes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules#post1043488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But page 185 on banes says that banes only cause lethal damage on spirits on twilight that arent manifested. Doesn't a spirit has to be manifested to BE in twilight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Twilight Form is technically a manifestation, yes. This is a poor choice of words. If a bane hits a spirit in Twilight it does lethal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules#post1043488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it also says manifested spirit touching the bane eat aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>That should be Materialized. Or Claimed. The rest of the Manifestations leave the entity in Twilight, I believe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules#post1043488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So that mean a werewolf cant kill a spirit permanently ever?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Drain it of Essence first. This is a requirement to kill one whether the spirit is in Twilight or the Hisil, it doesn't actually matter which.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules#post1043488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On page 184 on &quot;Spirit and Reaching&quot; sidebar it says spirit on a locus that matches its resonance heals twice as fast however i cant find how fast they normally heal.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they heal naturally I think it'd be at the rate other beings do. 1B/15Min 1L/2Days 1A/Week<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules#post1043488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About influences, how do they works. Says you got 3 in influences &quot;dog&quot; that means i can only do either:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Strengthen a dog &quot;1 minute per success&quot; (influence effect 1, duration 0)</li> <li>Strengthen a dog &quot;10 minute per success&quot; (influence effect 1, duration 1)</li> <li>Strengthen a dog &quot;1 Hour per success&quot; (influence effect 1, duration 2) and pay 1 additional essence</li> <li>Manipulate a dog &quot;1 minute per success&quot; (influence effect 2, duration 0)</li> <li>Manipulate a dog &quot;10 minute per success&quot; (influence effect 2, duration 1)</li> <li>Control a dog &quot;1 minute per success&quot; (Influence effect 3, duration 0)</li> </ol><br /> So that means a rank 5 spirit cant permanently create a example of its influence?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't really touch on this, I'm not great with the Influence system, but I think you have this right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules#post1043488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About Claimed, it says claimed gain influences of their spirit but loose the numina but can develop Dread powers. It doesnt say however how much dread power they gain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that's at ST discretion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules#post1043488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And finally the books seem to indicate that whenever it refers to a spirit materialize it truth it means a spirit is in twilight so it cant be seen by normal humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Materialized spirits are visible and physical, not in Twilight,<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T09:39:20-08:00","id":1043609,"title":"","content":"inodiv's got it. If you want to really kill a spirit, you have to drain it of Essence first, like by using their bane or a magical power or just tiring it out. It's worth keeping in mind there are other things a werewolf can do to a spirit, such as bind it in place or stick it in a fetish.<br /> <br /> As for Influences, they're more storyteller fiat, because there's basically billions of different kinds of Influences. But we've had a few threads on them that should help out, like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460187-four-dots-of-influence\">this</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/321704-explain-spirit-influences-to-me-like-i-m-5\">this</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40846-gmc-spirit-influences\">this</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/379105-is-werewolf-going-to-have-a-more-defined-version-of-influence\">this</a>.<br /> <br /> And yes, they heal like normal people. 'Spirits record and heal from wounds the same way as human characters, but in addition lose one point of Essence for every aggravated wound they suffer.' Though they can spend Essence to heal, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-04-2017, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T12:53:22-08:00","id":1043690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1043506#post1043506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules#post1043488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone.<br /> <i>On page 186 it says only spirits can be attack other spirits in twilight, does that mean a manifest spirit in invulnerable to werewolf attacks unless it outranks it or uses it banes?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry this confuses me because it seems spirits are kind of invincible then. They just have to stay invisible on the twilight, and even if they get detected by a werewolf and said werewolf can see in twilight (which i think is a specific gift?) by the time they get their bane and declare a hunt rite the spirit is gone. I though it was more &quot;see/suspect spirit, declare hunt, jump on the nearest locci into twilight and hunt it down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1043506#post1043506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Twilight Form is technically a manifestation, yes. This is a poor choice of words. If a bane hits a spirit in Twilight it does lethal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if the spirit is in hibernation? The spirit isnt using a manifestation but it is in twilight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1043506#post1043506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Drain it of Essence first. This is a requirement to kill one whether the spirit is in Twilight or the Hisil, it doesn't actually matter which.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok but how? I mean unless you outrank him werewolf claws only deal Bashing (even if he outrank the spirit, if it is on twilight then its only lethal to apparently) so one would need to hit overflow with enough successes in 1 roll as to fill their lethal and pass enough aggravated point to make them loose their essence. Otherwise they go into hibernation in twilight were they can only be attacked by other spirits no werewolves. <br /> <br /> I though it was a matter of getting the spirit into hibernation through loss of corpus and then finish the job in twilight but apparently i is not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1043506#post1043506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they heal naturally I think it'd be at the rate other beings do. 1B/15Min 1L/2Days 1A/Week</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1043609#post1043609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Influences, they're more storyteller fiat, because there's basically billions of different kinds of Influences. But we've had a few threads on them that should help out, like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460187-four-dots-of-influence\">this</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/321704-explain-spirit-influences-to-me-like-i-m-5\">this</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40846-gmc-spirit-influences\">this</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/379105-is-werewolf-going-to-have-a-more-defined-version-of-influence\">this</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup i read them but none of them answer my particular question. I get what Influences do or at least i got a headcannon of what they can do but what i dont quite get (my english is rusty) is whether with influences say influence 3 i get 3 dots to use <b><u>between</u></b> effect and duration. Or i get 3 dots to spend on effects and 3 dots to spend on duration?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T13:53:44-08:00","id":1043712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1043690#post1043690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry this confuses me because it seems spirits are kind of invincible then. They just have to stay invisible on the twilight, and even if they get detected by a werewolf and said werewolf can see in twilight (which i think is a specific gift?) by the time they get their bane and declare a hunt rite the spirit is gone. I though it was more &quot;see/suspect spirit, declare hunt, jump on the nearest locci into twilight and hunt it down.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a natural ability. If a spirit is in Twilight, and it's not actively hiding through some other means, a werewolf can see it. You don't need to have the spirit within sight to call a Siskur-Dah, or really need to even call a Siskur-Dah to fight a spirit. Werewolves have totems, spirit allies and other things that allow them to hurt spirits in Twilight, but for the most part a spirit just hanging around in Twilight isn't doing anything that warrants a hunt. In order to do more, it would need to invest more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if the spirit is in hibernation? The spirit isnt using a manifestation but it is in twilight. </div> </div> </div>They don't hibernate in Twilight. At least not for long. P184, 'When spirits enter hibernation in the physical world, they slowly move back across the Gauntlet into the Shadow, crossing over in the local Gauntlet\u2019s dice penalty in hours.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok but how? I mean unless you outrank him werewolf claws only deal Bashing (even if he outrank the spirit, if it is on twilight then its only lethal to apparently) so one would need to hit overflow with enough successes in 1 roll as to fill their lethal and pass enough aggravated point to make them loose their essence. Otherwise they go into hibernation in twilight were they can only be attacked by other spirits no werewolves. </div> </div> </div>As noted, spirits are not invulnerable to harm in Twilight. Worse comes to worse, for whatever reason the spirit is just standing in Twilight and being an annoyance, werewolves can use Twilight Purge and knock them out of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I though it was a matter of getting the spirit into hibernation through loss of corpus and then finish the job in twilight but apparently i is not? </div> </div> </div>Twilight isn't a place, it's an active state of ephemera in the real world and spirits don't naturally dwell in it. Existing in the gurihal, the real world, would drain Essence. Also p184, 'Spirits in the material world but outside of a suitable Condition bleed one point of Essence per hour.' A spirit just hanging around in Twilight would be draining unless they had a corresponding Condition or an active Fetter. And werewolves can deal with Conditions and Fetters. Also worth keeping in mind that they can find a spirit's bane and use that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yup i read them but none of them answer my particular question. I get what Influences do or at least i got a headcannon of what they can do but what i dont quite get (my english is rusty) is whether with influences say influence 3 i get 3 dots to use <b><u>between</u></b> effect and duration. Or i get 3 dots to spend on effects and 3 dots to spend on duration? </div> </div> </div>It's between them. Permanency requires great power, though you can make things last a long time just by spending Essence with your Successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T04:07:39-08:00","id":1043914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules#post1043488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So that means a rank 5 spirit cant permanently create a example of its influence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Trust me, this is a good thing. If Rank 5 spirits could trivially perma-create examples of their influence, the world would be buried in stuff popping out of no-where.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T06:17:15-08:00","id":1043943,"title":"","content":"Actually, the fifth Influence dot has a special rule that allows it to permanently create one example instead of mass creating several temporary examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T06:30:18-08:00","id":1043949,"title":"","content":"Hah, that teaches me for not rereading the Influence rules before posting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T15:07:23-08:00","id":1044206,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the clarifications i think i got it, except this one <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1043712#post1043712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't hibernate in Twilight. At least not for long. P184, 'When spirits enter hibernation in the physical world, they slowly move back across the Gauntlet into the Shadow, crossing over in the local Gauntlet\u2019s dice penalty in hours.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Because on<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Forsaken P186 </strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1043712#post1043712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits that lose all Corpus from lethal or aggravated wounds explode into bursts of ephemera stylized to their natures. For example, a forest spirit dies in a hail of rapidly vanishing pine needles. The spirit isn\u2019t actually dead, though, merely returned to dormancy unless it has also run out of Essence. If it has even a single Essence point remaining, it reforms in a safe place (a Resonant location, usually), hibernating.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this means a spirit that fills it Corpus track explodes into a burst of ephemera but then either instantaneously moves to a resonant location in the Hisil (P186) or it stays hibernating in twilight (maybe as a Spirit corpse), vulnerable to attacks, slowly while it moves to the shadows with the local gauntlet penalty in hours (P184)?<br /> <br /> As for banes do it got them right?<ul><li>If the bane is in the material world and the spirit is the Hisil nothing happens.</li> <li>If both bane and spirit are in the Hisil then the banes causes aggravated damage.</li> <li>If the bane is in the material world and the Spirit is in twilight then the banes causes lethal damage.</li> <li>If bane is in the material world and the spirit is fettered then the bane causes lethal to the spirit.</li> <li>If the bane is in the material world and the spirit is either possessing, a claimed or just used the &quot;materialize&quot; manifestation then it causes aggravated.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T15:45:02-08:00","id":1044232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1044206#post1044206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this means a spirit that fills it Corpus track explodes into a burst of ephemera but then either instantaneously moves to a resonant location in the Hisil (P186) or it stays hibernating in twilight (maybe as a Spirit corpse), vulnerable to attacks, slowly while it moves to the shadows with the local gauntlet penalty in hours (P184)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Upon death, it reforms in a safe place, hibernating. It doesn't hibernate, allowing you to attack it, then teleport to a safe place, it's the other way around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for banes do it got them right?<ul><li>If the bane is in the material world and the spirit is the Hisil nothing happens.</li> <li>If both bane and spirit are in the Hisil then the banes causes aggravated damage.</li> <li>If the bane is in the material world and the Spirit is in twilight then the banes causes lethal damage.</li> <li>If bane is in the material world and the spirit is fettered then the bane causes lethal to the spirit.</li> <li>If the bane is in the material world and the spirit is either possessing, a claimed or just used the &quot;materialize&quot; manifestation then it causes aggravated.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> Yes.<br /> Yes, though you could conceivably have a bane weapon that's enhanced to act as if it's in Twilight, whereupon it would inflict Aggravated.<br /> Sort of. That's if the bane is touching the thing the spirit is Fettered to. Otherwise a Fettered spirit in Twilight acts as the rule above.<br /> Yes, except with Possess. With Possess the spirit is in Twilight, but 'superimposed' over the subject of Possession, so it follows the rules above for a spirit in Twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T05:14:28-08:00","id":1044999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1043914#post1043914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Trust me, this is a good thing. If Rank 5 spirits could trivially perma-create examples of their influence, the world would be buried in stuff popping out of no-where.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was my understanding rank 5 spirits are Rare? Like, 10 per country or so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T08:09:04-08:00","id":1045064,"title":"","content":"Way, way more common than that. <br /> <br /> Though you're free to make them as rare as you want, the setting has them pretty common. At least one for every town that isn't dead or dying, and multiples for every major city. Events that tainted the area, like Gettysburg, monuments or particularly noteworthy geographical features like big lakes or rivers. In London the spirit of the Tube, for instance. Ancient gods that are no longer worshiped or servitors of current gods.<br /> <br /> First edition focused more on low-to-mid power, so we didn't get many named and written up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-07-2017, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T16:53:18-08:00","id":1045493,"title":"","content":"Rank 5 spirits appear to be rare because most of them are either sleeping, or unable to cross over into the physical world. I imagine most of them chilling out in the Deep Shadows of their own making.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Well, actually that's close to Rank 6+ spirits. But still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T18:13:02-08:00","id":1046097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1044232#post1044232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Upon death, it reforms in a safe place, hibernating. It doesn't hibernate, allowing you to attack it, then teleport to a safe place, it's the other way around.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes.<br /> Yes.<br /> Yes, though you could conceivably have a bane weapon that's enhanced to act as if it's in Twilight, whereupon it would inflict Aggravated.<br /> Sort of. That's if the bane is touching the thing the spirit is Fettered to. Otherwise a Fettered spirit in Twilight acts as the rule above.<br /> Yes, except with Possess. With Possess the spirit is in Twilight, but 'superimposed' over the subject of Possession, so it follows the rules above for a spirit in Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1043609#post1043609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for Influences, they're more storyteller fiat, because there's basically billions of different kinds of Influences. But we've had a few threads on them that should help out, like <a href=\"http://&quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460187-four-dots-of-influence&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> and <a href=\"http://&quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/321704-explain-spirit-influences-to-me-like-i-m-5&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> and <a href=\"http://&quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40846-gmc-spirit-influences&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> and <a href=\"http://&quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/379105-is-werewolf-going-to-have-a-more-defined-version-of-influence&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have another question about influences. I couldnt find how much of a bonus strenghten influence gives beyond for the specific case of health (+rank in health). How strenghten works for things like defense or attributes? <br /> <br /> +rank in attributes or defense? Or allocating successes on the roll? The second one would be weird as it would be the only influence that allocates successes to effect when normally are use to duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 02-08-2017, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T18:14:11-08:00","id":1046098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1044999#post1044999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was my understanding rank 5 spirits are Rare? Like, 10 per country or so?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they should be more as rank 6-7 entities creates them too as royal avatars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T18:38:57-08:00","id":1046107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1046097#post1046097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have another question about influences. I couldnt find how much of a bonus strenghten influence gives beyond for the specific case of health (+rank in health). How strenghten works for things like defense or attributes?<br /> <br /> +rank in attributes or defense? Or allocating successes on the roll? The second one would be weird as it would be the only influence that allocates successes to effect when normally are use to duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>In first addition it was by Rank. So you'd add Rank to Defense or rolls with Influence-relevant Attribute. You could justify allocating successes on the roll if it was a spirit of a particular skill, I think, and perhaps using Manipulate or Control. Influence stuff is fairly ST-mandated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T12:19:51-08:00","id":1046415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1046107#post1046107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In first addition it was by Rank. So you'd add Rank to Defense or rolls with Influence-relevant Attribute. You could justify allocating successes on the roll if it was a spirit of a particular skill, I think, and perhaps using Manipulate or Control. Influence stuff is fairly ST-mandated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the clarification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T12:24:57-08:00","id":1046417,"title":"","content":"Regarding the destruction of a spirit, the rite Sacred Hunt (page 140) allows the werewolfs to consume the remaining esscence of the prey, and it can be used to destroy a spirit. As I understand it, if the prey of a sacred hunt is a spirit and the pack brings it down, they can consume all its remaining esscence, either after or before it discorporates, which destroys it (if it's done after discorporation) or gives the perfect chance to destroy it. It is worth noting that this can only be donde in the Hisil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3456-sir-phobos","user":"Sir Phobos","date":". 02-09-2017, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3456-sir-phobos","name":"Sir Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T12:32:11-08:00","id":1046420,"title":"","content":"Absolutely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T23:08:41-08:00","id":1046650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sir Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1046417#post1046417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is worth noting that this can only be donde in the Hisil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless I'm misremembering the Sacred Hunt rules and Condition, nothing says this is limited to the Hisil.<br /> <br /> In fact, it makes more thematic sense if it isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 02-10-2017, 03:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T04:26:07-08:00","id":1046711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1046650#post1046650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless I'm misremembering the Sacred Hunt rules and Condition, nothing says this is limited to the Hisil.<br /> <br /> In fact, it makes more thematic sense if it isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could start the rite in the material world but unless the ritemaster is a Bone shadow, whose Sacred hunt lets you hit ephemeral being in the material (though i doesnt say whether that mean spirits in twilight or in the hisil), then you would need to cross over. If i understand it right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T05:12:40-08:00","id":1046719,"title":"","content":"Sacred Hunt specifically doesn't require a kill, it just needs the spirit to be &quot;brought down&quot;. There's a multitude of ways to do this that don't require having a Bone Shadow rite master or being in the Hisil. Gifts, rites, banes, the totem, bargaining with allied spirits or more powerful spirits, fetishes, etc. You could even just trick the prey spirit into surrendering (bringing it down) and then unmake it as empowered to do by the Sacred Hunt rite. (Expect word of such dishonest behaviour to spread among spirits if the pack does resort to this kind of trickery.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T08:10:02-08:00","id":1046772,"title":"","content":"Plus as we've discussed there are ways to hit ephemeral beings in the gurihal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T20:39:50-08:00","id":1047525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1046719#post1046719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sacred Hunt specifically doesn't require a kill, it just needs the spirit to be &quot;brought down&quot;. There's a multitude of ways to do this that don't require having a Bone Shadow rite master or being in the Hisil. Gifts, rites, banes, the totem, bargaining with allied spirits or more powerful spirits, fetishes, etc. You could even just trick the prey spirit into surrendering (bringing it down) and then unmake it as empowered to do by the Sacred Hunt rite. (Expect word of such dishonest behaviour to spread among spirits if the pack does resort to this kind of trickery.)</div> </div> </div> </div>But that would kill it permanently? For a spirit to die one needs to take away all his essence and loose all corpus. The sacred hunt rite just lets you drain a spirit by &quot;bringing it down&quot; but unless you also make it loose all its corpus (with rites, gifts to hit him in the hisil or spirit allies) it wont kill it permantely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T22:10:04-08:00","id":1047553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1047525#post1047525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that would kill it permanently? For a spirit to die one needs to take away all his essence and loose all corpus. The sacred hunt rite just lets you drain a spirit by &quot;bringing it down&quot; but unless you also make it loose all its corpus (with rites, gifts to hit him in the hisil or spirit allies) it wont kill it permantely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Draining the spirit of all its Essence after bringing it down through the sacred hunt specifically discorporates and destroys it permanently. Corpus is irrelevant to the rite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T05:30:21-08:00","id":1047664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1047553#post1047553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Draining the spirit of all its Essence after bringing it down through the sacred hunt specifically discorporates and destroys it permanently. Corpus is irrelevant to the rite.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;If the Uratha bring down a spirit that is the prey of this rite, they may divide its remaining Essence amongst themselves as they see fit; this can be used to destroy a spirit by draining all its Essence and discorporating it, but doing so is usually a breaking point toward Spirit and is seen as disrespectful if done without good reason.&quot;<br /> <br /> Its probably my bad english but it isnt very clear if this refers that any kind of &quot;bringing it down&quot; will automatically drain of it all essence and discorporate the spirit thus destroying it. Or that it can be used alongside bringing it down through violent means to destroy it. The whole line of &quot;this can be used to destroy a spirit by draining.....&quot; got me confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T02:29:13-08:00","id":1048136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1047664#post1047664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;If the Uratha bring down a spirit that is the prey of this rite, they may divide its remaining Essence amongst themselves as they see fit; this can be used to destroy a spirit by draining all its Essence and discorporating it, but doing so is usually a breaking point toward Spirit and is seen as disrespectful if done without good reason.&quot;<br /> <br /> Its probably my bad english but it isnt very clear if this refers that any kind of &quot;bringing it down&quot; will automatically drain of it all essence and discorporate the spirit thus destroying it. Or that it can be used alongside bringing it down through violent means to destroy it. The whole line of &quot;this can be used to destroy a spirit by draining.....&quot; got me confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bBringing down a spirit does not automatically drain and destroy it; that's a choice on the part of the Uratha to do so. The key words here are 'may' and 'can', indicating that the option is there for the Uratha but that it is not compulsory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T02:48:12-08:00","id":1048141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1048136#post1048136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bBringing down a spirit does not automatically drain and destroy it; that's a choice on the part of the Uratha to do so. The key words here are 'may' and 'can', indicating that the option is there for the Uratha but that it is not compulsory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I was just about to post the same <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T09:58:52-08:00","id":1051036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules#post1043488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone.<br /> However on page 186 says that physical attacks on manifest spirits (meaning in twilight right?) or in the hisil deal only bashing. So unless you (a werewolf) outrank the spirit or uses its banes the only way to fill that track is by overflowing its corpus track with bashing until it also becomes lethal?<br /> <br /> On page 186 it says only spirits can be attack other spirits in twilight, does that mean a manifest spirit in invulnerable to werewolf attacks unless it outranks it or uses it banes? But page 185 on banes says that banes only cause lethal damage on spirits on twilight that arent manifested. Doesn't a spirit has to be manifested to BE in twilight? Because it also says manifested spirit touching the bane eat aggravated damage.<br /> Thanks for any answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>sorry guys, i can t understand this one..<br /> so, to be in twilight form they have to be manifested.. according to the combat paragraph, in twilight, a spirit can only be attacked by other spirits or their banes... but after, in the same combat chapter, is written that normal attacks that cause lethal damage, just deal bashing damage<br /> so, if a spirit is not in hisil, means that is manifested in the real world; now, to damage him, you need a bane or outrank him. Plus, wich of 2 paragraphes is right?? the first or second??<br /> because if the first is right, means you cannot attack the spirit at all without the right bane (or rank)<br /> if the second is right.. what the hell the first sentence means?? because in this case you only need bane to inflict lethal damage(or rank)<br /> <br /> and another stuff: in twilight ( so, when they are manifested), if they are not using manifestation= image, they are invisible to anybody<br /> but, according to page 95 (spirit sense), a werewolf can sense a spirit in twilight.. this means that the werewolf can see him?? touch him?? hear him?? or just detect his presence like a sixth sense??<br /> thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T10:11:39-08:00","id":1051043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1051036#post1051036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">sorry guys, i can t understand this one..<br /> so, to be in twilight form they have to be manifested.. according to the combat paragraph, in twilight, a spirit can only be attacked by other spirits or their banes... but after, in the same combat chapter, is written that normal attacks that cause lethal damage, just deal bashing damage</div> </div> </div> </div>The Materialize Manifestation makes a spirit solid in the material world for its duration and being in the Shadow does not change the way combat works when dealing with spirits besides removing Twilight as a concern. Hitting a Gaffling with a meat cleaver isn't going to deal much in the way of damage, but it <i>will</i> deal damage on a successful hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T05:20:46-08:00","id":1052510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1051036#post1051036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> sorry guys, i can t understand this one..<br /> so, to be in twilight form they have to be manifested.. according to the combat paragraph, in twilight, a spirit can only be attacked by other spirits or their banes... but after, in the same combat chapter, is written that normal attacks that cause lethal damage, just deal bashing damage<br /> so, if a spirit is not in hisil, means that is manifested in the real world; now, to damage him, you need a bane or outrank him. Plus, wich of 2 paragraphes is right?? the first or second??<br /> because if the first is right, means you cannot attack the spirit at all without the right bane (or rank)<br /> if the second is right.. what the hell the first sentence means?? because in this case you only need bane to inflict lethal damage(or rank)</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I understand it, it works like this: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px; width: 416px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>World</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>State of spirit</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Damage from bane</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Physical damage</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Gurihal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Twilight</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Lethal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">None</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Gurihal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Materialized</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Aggravated</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Bashing</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Hisil</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">-</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Aggravated</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Bashing</td> </tr> </table></div> Some rituals, like the sacred hunt performed by Shadow Bones, <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">allow the werewolfs to attack a spirit in twilight as if it is materialized.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1051036#post1051036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and another stuff: in twilight ( so, when they are manifested), if they are not using manifestation= image, they are invisible to anybody<br /> but, according to page 95 (spirit sense), a werewolf can sense a spirit in twilight.. this means that the werewolf can see him?? touch him?? hear him?? or just detect his presence like a sixth sense??<br /> thank you</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> I think in some places it should say materialized instead of manifested. When they are in twilight they are invisible and untouchable by anything that\u2019s not a spirit, but the spirit senses of the werewolf allow them to sense it. I understand it as the werewolf being able to see and hear it but not touch it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3456-sir-phobos","user":"Sir Phobos","date":". 02-21-2017, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3456-sir-phobos","name":"Sir Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T05:27:59-08:00","id":1052511,"title":"","content":"It's a terminology problem. Twilight Form is called a Manifestation, but almost everytime a book says Manifestations or Manifested it excludes Twilight Form. It's especially ridiculous in Mage where there is a type of ephemeral entity that does not have any Manifestations but can still be summoned to the Material/Gurihal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T05:34:52-08:00","id":1052514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1043488-question-about-spirit-rules?p=1052511#post1052511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a terminology problem. Twilight Form is called a Manifestation, but almost everytime a book says Manifestations or Manifested it excludes Twilight Form. It's especially ridiculous in Mage where there is a type of ephemeral entity that does not have any Manifestations but can still be summoned to the Material/Gurihal.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is mentioned that Twilight Form is the only manifestation that Goetia have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T05:58:17-08:00","id":1052524,"title":"","content":"&quot;Spirits and ghosts begin with the Twilight Form Manifestation <br /> and a number of Manifestation Effects from the list below equal <br /> to Rank. [..]<br /> Goetia do not naturally possess Manifestations.&quot;<br /> Page 258 in Mage.<br /> Goetia do enter Twilight when summoned as stated elsewhere, but my point was that the gamelines suffer from broken terminology since Twilight Form is said to be a Manifestation, but is never treated as one by the rules.<br /> <br /> Edit: So basically anytime the books mentions &quot;Manifestation(s)&quot; exclude Twilight Form, and when they mention &quot;Manifested&quot; it's usually Materialized and not any other Manifestation since most Manifestations still has the entity remain in Twilight Form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-21-2017, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T06:19:46-08:00","id":1052531,"title":"","content":"thank you<br /> in the end, i understood theese rules well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> just a detail: the hisil is the shadow realm for werewolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T08:07:09-08:00","id":1052577,"title":"","content":"Yes. The Hisil is the Shadow, it's the name in the First Tongue, the language of spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T08:48:03-08:00","id":1053243,"title":"","content":"Goetia can't normally get into twilight by themselves at all, so technically counting twilight form as a manifestation doesn't contradict the statement that they don't naturally have any.<br /> <br /> It's a sort of default null-manifestation. Technically is one, but doesn't really count for most purposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}